@startuml pipeline
title Pipeline — degradation models the residual that preprocessing did not remove

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<cache>> LightYellow
  BackgroundColor<<deg>> MistyRose
  BackgroundColor<<train>> Honeydew
  BackgroundColor<<eval>> AliceBlue
}

rectangle "PPM crop\n25x25 .. 266x266" as ppm
rectangle "preprocessing\nto_gray / to_hsv\nresize 48x48\nCLAHE" as prep
rectangle "cache .npy\n48x48 uint8, CLEAN\nthe only persisted artifact" as cache <<cache>>

ppm --> prep
prep --> cache

rectangle "train 31,379\ntrack-disjoint" as tr <<train>>
rectangle "val 7,830" as va <<train>>
rectangle "select k, C, class_weight\nby val macro-F1" as sel <<train>>
rectangle "fit representation\nPCA | HOG | BoVW | CNN\n+ LinearSVC" as fit <<train>>
cache --> tr : read train
cache --> va : read val
va --> sel
sel ..> fit : chosen\nhyperparameters
tr --> fit

rectangle "test\n12,630" as te <<eval>>
rectangle "degradations.apply\nnoise / blur / gamma\n<b>on the model input</b>" as deg <<deg>>
rectangle "transform + classify" as clf <<eval>>
rectangle "results.csv" as res <<eval>>

cache --> te : read test
te --> deg
deg --> clf
fit ..> clf : fitted model, no retraining
clf --> res

note right of deg
  Injected <b>after</b> preprocessing, so it is by
  construction the degradation preprocessing
  did <b>not</b> remove -- the residual the
  representation must cope with.
  One level = one condition, independent of
  sign size and of preprocessing config.
end note

note bottom of tr
  Training is always clean.
  No augmentation, no degradation.
  Fit on train only, never train+val:
  the CNN needs val for early stopping.
end note
@enduml
